3:["$","p","For horizontal blinds, close them in one",{"children":"For horizontal blinds, close them in one direction, dust, then reverse and dust again to reach both sides of each slat. This simple routine prevents dust buildup that leads to more intensive cleaning needs."}]
4:["$","div","2",{"className":"flex flex-col items-start","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-heading text-[18px] font-semibold leading-[27px] tracking-[-0.0648px] text-navy","children":"3. Deep Cleaning Techniques"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-4 flex flex-col gap-[23px] text-[16px] leading-[23px] text-navy","children":[["$","p","When regular dusting is no longer enough",{"children":"When regular dusting is no longer enough, it's time for a deeper clean. Remove blinds from their brackets and lay them flat on a clean surface or hang them on a clothesline outdoors."}],["$","p","For non-fabric treatments, fill a bathtu",{"children":"For non-fabric treatments, fill a bathtub or large basin with warm water and a few drops of mild dish soap. Submerge the blinds and let them soak for 15-20 minutes. Use a soft sponge to gently scrub each slat, paying extra attention to the bottom slats that collect the most grime."}],["$","p","Rinse thoroughly with clean water and al",{"children":"Rinse thoroughly with clean water and allow to dry completely before rehanging. Never rehang damp blinds, as trapped moisture can promote mold growth — especially important in Florida's humid environment."}]]}]]}]
5:["$","div","3",{"className":"grid grid-cols-1 gap-3 md:grid-cols-3","children":[["$","div","Cleaning supplies arranged for blind maintenance",{"className":"relative h-[240px] overflow-hidden rounded-lg md:h-[280px] xl:h-[359px]","children":["$","$L2",null,{"src":"/images/resources/knowledge-grid-1.webp","alt":"Cleaning supplies arranged for blind maintenance","fill":true,"className":"object-cover"}]}],["$","div","Freshly cleaned roller shades in a bedroom",{"className":"relative h-[240px] overflow-hidden rounded-lg md:h-[280px] xl:h-[359px]","children":["$","$L2",null,{"src":"/images/resources/knowledge-grid-2.webp","alt":"Freshly cleaned roller shades in a bedroom","fill":true,"className":"object-cover"}]}],["$","div","Professional deep cleaning of fabric drapes",{"className":"relative h-[240px] overflow-hidden rounded-lg md:h-[280px] xl:h-[359px]","children":["$","$L2",null,{"src":"/images/resources/knowledge-grid-3.webp","alt":"Professional deep cleaning of fabric drapes","fill":true,"className":"object-cover"}]}]]}]
6:["$","div","4",{"className":"flex flex-col items-start","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-heading text-[18px] font-semibold leading-[27px] tracking-[-0.0648px] text-navy","children":"4. When to Call a Professional"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-4 flex flex-col gap-[23px] text-[16px] leading-[23px] text-navy","children":[["$","p","Some cleaning jobs are best left to prof",{"children":"Some cleaning jobs are best left to professionals. Delicate fabrics, motorized systems with integrated components, and heavily soiled treatments may require specialized equipment and expertise."}],["$","p","Professional cleaning services use ultra",{"children":"Professional cleaning services use ultrasonic cleaning technology that can remove deep-set dirt without the agitation that damages delicate materials. They can also treat stains, apply UV protectants, and identify early signs of wear."}],["$","p","As a rule of thumb, if your window treat",{"children":"As a rule of thumb, if your window treatments haven't been cleaned in over a year, or if you notice persistent odors or visible staining, a professional cleaning is a worthwhile investment."}]]}]]}]
